      "rationale": "🩹️ RECLASSIFIED (ticket SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION, shard A10, 2026-09-02). This entry was registered `third-party-library` on the strength of a real crate that does genuine codec work, but the mutation's expected RESULT is computed by this owner's own `🦀️oracle.rs` -- its dispatch function's catch-all arm is `\"mutation kind {...} has no oracle implementation\"`, proof that every OTHER arm is an implementation, not a reading. Both halves of the comparison then descend from the same specification, so a shared misreading produces two agreeing wrong answers -- the one failure a differential oracle exists to catch. This is a `cross-semio-implementation`: a required SUPPLEMENT (metamorphic/inverse/round-trip evidence), never a substitute. A qualifying third-party reference for the mutation semantics is still owed. See $TICKET/📓️a10-oracle-honesty.md.\n\nruststep 0.4 (newly linked this wave) is a real, actively-maintained ISO 10303-21/-11 (EXPRESS) parser for Rust -- confirmed by reading its own source (~/.cargo/registry/src/.../ruststep-0.4.0): `ast::Exchange`/`ast::DataSection`/`ast::Record`/`ast::Parameter`/`ast::EntityInstance` all implement `FromStr` over the real Part-21 clear-text grammar (multi-line records, nested lists, typed/complex instances, `$`/`*`/`.ENUM.`/`#ref` tokens), verified against this subset's own real fixture (1396 real entities parsed with zero errors). It has NO writer at all: `ast::ser::to_record` only builds a `Record` from an already-typed Rust struct (schema-generated ap201/ap203 tables this crate does not even compile, since AP214 has no generated schema module in ruststep at all), and grepping the whole crate source for `Display`/`fmt::Formatter` impls on `Exchange`/`DataSection`/`Record`/`Parameter` finds none -- there is no `to_string`/serialize path back to Part-21 text anywhere in the crate. Per the fleet brief's §6, this rules out `@mode-differential`: ruststep cannot be a second PRODUCER of mutated bytes to diff against. It is registered here strictly as the INDEPENDENT READER role instead -- every real mutation this subset's own oracle dispatcher (`../🦀️oracle.rs`) performs (via ruststep's real parse plus this module's own from-scratch Part-21 writer, since none exists to reuse) is read back through a FRESH, independent `ruststep::ast::Exchange::from_str` call before being projected onto `semantic-step-v1`, and the identity round trip is checked the same way. This is real third-party evidence about the STRUCTURE of the result (entity graph shape, header schema, argument values as ruststep's own parser sees them), even though it cannot discharge a byte-level differential claim.",
      "hostPath": "✏️s/🔌️plugins/🗄️stdio/🧪️oracle/📦️packages/🦀️rust",
